  "semantics": "First line n, 1<=n<=10^5; then n lines \"k_i a_i\", 0<=k_i<=10^9 distinct, 1<=a_i<=10^9: a_i boxes of side 2^(k_i). A box fits inside any strictly larger box, so boxes nest. Equal-size boxes cannot nest, hence a box of side 2^p holds at most 4^(p-k) boxes of side 2^k (area) and needs p>k; quadtree-aligned placement achieves this for every size simultaneously because each placed box re-exposes its own cell. Unique answer p = max_i (k_i + max(1, ceil(log4 a_i))), one integer. Checked against bottom-up level carrying and top-down slot-feasibility brutes.",
